# Force LF line endings for Zebra source files on all platforms.
# The Zebra tokenizer only handles LF; CRLF causes error.UnexpectedCharacter.
*.zbr text eol=lf

# Zig sources and the build manifest too. build.zig locates the preamble sections by
# marker strings; a CRLF checkout (Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true) broke
# the release workflow on 2026-09-12. LF everywhere, no exceptions.
*.zig text eol=lf
*.zon text eol=lf

# Generated Zig artifacts. These MUST stay tracked — they are the bootstrap seed
# (a self-hosted compiler needs a compiler to build itself). But they are machine
# output, not hand-written source: 16% of their lines are `// zbr:file:N` markers
# that renumber on any shift, so a 57-line .zbr edit rewrites ~22,000 lines.
# `-diff` keeps that noise out of diffs/logs (use `git diff --text` to see it);
# `linguist-generated` keeps it out of GitHub review and language stats.
selfhost/*.zig linguist-generated=true -diff

# Documentation. Not a correctness hazard the way .zbr is (nothing tokenizes a
# .md), but a CRLF rewrite of a large ledger produces a diff in which EVERY line
# has changed -- BUGS.md turned up on 2026-08-05 as 1,597 insertions and 1,508
# deletions for what was a 90-line addition. That is not cosmetic: it makes the
# real change unreviewable, and review is the only control on an append-only
# record. Normalising here fixes it for whoever writes next, rather than asking
# every tool and every author to remember.
*.md text eol=lf
